      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion! I don\u0027t think this applies here though -- we publish via the com.vanniktech.maven.publish Gradle plugin (configured in kmp-money/build.gradle.kts), not a plain `mvn deploy`. That plugin talks to the Central Portal API directly and reads credentials from Gradle properties (mavenCentralUsername/mavenCentralPassword), which Jenkins supplies as ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_* environment variables that Gradle maps automatically. There\u0027s no ~/.m2/settings.xml / Nexus staging flow in this pipeline, so a settings-ci.xml server block wouldn\u0027t be read by anything here. This is documented in PUBLISHING.md (section 3, \"Jenkins credentials\").",
